&lt;p&gt;Sentinel Defense Systems develops secure communications and mission-planning software for U.S. Department of Defense and intelligence community customers. Our Huntsville, Alabama engineering center is hiring a Junior Software Engineer for the Mission Data team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Develop and test TypeScript and Java components for a mission-planning web application deployed on classified networks.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Write unit and integration tests and support system-level verification events.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Document software changes according to DoD configuration-management processes.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Basic qualifications (required)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An active U.S. Secret security clearance&lt;/strong&gt; at the time of application. We cannot sponsor a clearance for this position.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;U.S. citizenship is required&lt;/strong&gt; as a condition of the clearance.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;A bachelor's degree in Computer Science or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;0-2 years of software development experience.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Ability to work on site in Huntsville, AL five days a week. This role is not eligible for remote work.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Experience with Node.js, React or Spring Boot.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;Security+ or another DoD 8570 baseline certification.&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Salary range: USD 72,000-88,000. Sentinel Defense Systems is an equal opportunity employer. U.S. citizenship and an active clearance are required due to the nature of the work.&lt;/p&gt;
